g as far as to  accuse the director of trying to ruin  his career by making him star  opposite something so ridiculous  letterier goaded worthington by saying  he wasn't trying to ruin his career  just damage it which didn't exactly help  matters  ultimately to appease his star leteriae  took the owl out of the film  relegating it to a brief cameo shrek  shrek's signature scottish accent went  through a couple of major changes before  audiences fell in love with the big  green ogre  saturday night live vet chris farley was  originally supposed to voice the  character but passed away before he  could finish recording his lines  after his passing mike myers stepped in  it wasn't until after roughly a third of  the movie had been animated however that  myers decided shrek should be scottish  meyer's reasoning was that since the  movie's villain lord farquaad spoke with  an upper class english accent shrek  should sound more blue-collar  to highlight the difference between them  it's  hideous oh that's not very nice  it's just a donkey he also felt that the  scottish accent lent itself better to  dramatic abrupt shifts in tone and would  allow him to emote in a more exaggerated  fashion  dreamworks exec jeffrey katzenberg  pegged the cost of reworking the already  animated scenes at four to five million  dollars  roughly 10 percent of the movie's  overall budget star wars attack of the  clones  after watching a rough cut of the battle  for geonosis with star wars creator  george lucas  samuel l jackson noticed it was hard to  spot his own character mace windu  amongst the dozens of jedi on screen  he asked lucas if it would be possible  for windu to wield a purple lightsaber  partly because it did stand out more and  partly because purple is jackson's  favorite color  i said to george you think maybe i can  get a purple lightsaber  lightsabers are green and lightsabers  are in them yeah but i want a purple one  lucas initially turned down the request  but later decided 